# The rendezvous image builds ONLY the Go relay node (see infra/rendezvous/
# Dockerfile: `go build ./cmd/rendezvous`), so the build context is a
# WHITELIST: everything is excluded, then the few trees the build actually
# reads are let back in.
#
# It used to be a blocklist, and a blocklist here loses by default: every new
# artifact directory (dist-release/ at 404MB, the Android build at 1.4GB) was
# silently included until someone noticed a 700MB upload and went looking.
# With a whitelist, new bloat costs nothing unless it lands inside one of the
# four entries below — and nothing but source belongs in those.

*

# Module definition, including the replace directive that makes the vendored
# MLS fork below resolve.
!go.mod
!go.sum

# The relay itself (its embedded guest page lives in cmd/rendezvous/guestpage,
# so it rides along here).
!cmd

# Packages the relay imports.
!internal
!third_party
